<p>The self‑attested RC photocopy confirms the vehicle’s legal ownership and registration details. A current PUC certificate proves the car meets environmental safety standards, which is mandatory for inter‑state transport. The insurance certificate must be valid for the entire transit period and cover both the vehicle and any cargo it carries.</p>
<p>The IBA‑approved consignment bilty is a specialized transport document that records the vehicle’s condition, route, and responsible parties. It serves as a legal proof of delivery and is required for customs clearance when crossing state borders. Transporters must retain a copy of this bilty in their records and provide a counterpart to the vehicle owner.</p>
<p>In addition to the above, it is highly recommended to secure <strong>100 % declared‑value marine transit insurance</strong>. This coverage guarantees full reimbursement for the vehicle’s market value in the event of loss, theft, or damage during sea or rail transit.</p>
<p>Marine transit insurance is a critical safeguard, especially for high‑value or luxury vehicles, and it protects against unforeseen incidents that could otherwise result in substantial financial loss.</p>
<p>By assembling these documents and opting for comprehensive marine transit insurance, vehicle owners can confidently proceed with transportation in Khunti, knowing they meet all regulatory requirements and are fully protected against potential risks.</p></div>
